# Skills Quick Reference

| Task | Skill | Key Rules |
|------|-------|-----------|
| Backend API, handlers, services, domain | `go-backend` | architecture, go-style-guide |
| REST/HTTP endpoint design, URL structure, status codes | `rest-api-design` | architecture, go-style-guide, authentication-security |
| Schema changes, migrations | `database-migrations` | database-migrations |
| React components, frontend UI | `frontend-react` | frontend-patterns |
| Writing/fixing tests, coverage | `testing` | go-testing-practices, frontend-testing-practices, e2e-testing-standards, testing-agent |
| TDD cycle details, examples | `tdd-workflow` | test-driven-development |
| Requirements, acceptance criteria | `user-stories` | - |
| Clean code principles | `clean-code` | go-style-guide |
| Commit messages, PR/squash titles, conventional commits | `conventional-commits` | agent-behavior |
| Stage and create git commits (Conventional Commits) | `git-commit` | conventional-commits, agent-behavior |
| Stress-test a plan or design (on request only) | `grilling` | - |
| Domain terms, `GLOSSARY.md`, ADRs in `docs/adr/` | `domain-modeling` | architecture |
| Conversation to PRD as a GitHub issue | `to-prd` | - |
| PRD or plan to tracer-bullet GitHub issues | `to-issues` | - |
| Bug, failure, or performance regression | `diagnosing-bugs` | test-driven-development, testing-agent |
| Review a branch or PR against standards and spec | `code-review` | all applicable rules |
| Write a PR body | `pr` | - |
| Steps only a human can do (secrets, dashboards, cutovers) | `wizard` | - |
| Untrusted input, auth, secrets, dependencies | `security-and-hardening` | authentication-security |
| Logging, metrics, tracing, alerts | `observability-and-instrumentation` | - |
| Pre-launch gate, rollout, rollback | `shipping-and-launch` | - |
| Hand work to a fresh agent (on request only) | `handoff` | - |

Skills are in `../skills/<name>/SKILL.md` (relative to `rules/`; at repo root: `skills/<name>/SKILL.md`)

## Workflows

- **Greenfield:** `grilling` → `domain-modeling` → `to-prd` → `to-issues` → build test-first → `security-and-hardening` → `observability-and-instrumentation` → `shipping-and-launch` → `pr`
- **Brownfield:** pstack `/how` or `/why` → `domain-modeling` to record existing terms → `diagnosing-bugs` or `/poteto-mode` → `code-review` → `pr`

## How to Use Skills

1. Check the table above for your task type
2. Read the skill file for detailed instructions
3. Follow references to relevant rules as needed

